# On Information Retrieval (IR) Systems: Revisiting Their Development, Evaluation Methodologies, and Assumptions (SIGs LAN, ED).

**Authors:** Stirling, Keith

## Abstract
Describes a session on information retrieval systems that planned to discuss relevance measures with Web-based information retrieval; retrieval system performance and evaluation; probabilistic independence of index terms; vector-based models; metalanguages and digital objects; how users assess the reliability, timeliness and bias of information; and changing theoretical perspectives of digital libraries (LRW)

**Source:** https://eric.ed.gov/?id=EJ618432

